gst-wayland-display: give each CUDAContext wrapper its own reference

Applies on top of games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display 016b4fc (GST_WAYLAND_DISPLAY_REF in
docker/wolf.Dockerfile). Wolf ticket XERK-1740; vendored here in XERK-2487 so the image no
longer needs the xerktech/gst-wayland-display fork.

An application that answers waylanddisplaysrc's NEED_CONTEXT with a CUDA context it keeps for
every pipeline (Wolf caches one per process) lost one reference to it per pipeline, until the
context was finalized under a live pipeline (`GST_IS_CUDA_CONTEXT` / `ref_count > 0`
assertions, then a frozen stream or a SIGSEGV in cuStreamDestroy). The answer re-enters
set_context() while new_from_gstreamer() is still inside gst_cuda_ensure_element_context(), and
adopt_slot_ref() could not tell that from the helper creating the context itself. The slot now
owns the helpers' reference (released with the element) and every wrapper takes its own.

Upstream: the same ownership rule is in games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display PR #70 (72922fe),
which is not yet in stable. Drop this patch once the Wolf image builds an upstream release that
has it.

